{"title":"2000 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be coprime positive integers such that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d1580235bf4edf4971a1d9ac08688804455a85c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{p}{q}=1-\\frac12+\\frac13-\\frac14 \\cdots -\\dfrac{1}{1334}+\\dfrac{1}{1335}\\]\" width=\"299\" height=\"40\" />\nProve that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b910f4dafca80b54c6e7bedf63b6485eebff0764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{p}{q}&amp;=1-\\frac12+\\frac13-\\frac14 \\cdots -\\dfrac{1}{1334}+\\dfrac{1}{1335}\\\\\n&amp;=\\sum_{k=1}^{1335}\\left(\\dfrac1k\\right)-2\\sum_{i=1}^{667}\\left(\\frac1{2i}\\right)\\\\\n&amp;=\\sum_{k=1}^{1335}\\left(\\dfrac1k\\right)-\\sum_{i=1}^{667}\\left(\\frac1{i}\\right)\\\\\n&amp;=\\sum_{m=668}^{1335}\\left(\\frac1m\\right).\\\\\n\\end{align*}\nNotice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c21503e4cc902ae41363360fd62e79f7402f7b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$668+1335=2003$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"15\" />, so we can pair up every term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79f244d658a9f15bbc070ea1eba561eb010aada6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003-m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> and rewrite this summation as\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sum_{m=668}^{1335}\\left(\\frac1m\\right)&amp;=\\sum_{m=668}^{1001}\\left(\\frac1m+\\frac1{2003-m}\\right)\\\\\n&amp;=\\sum_{m=668}^{1001}\\left(\\frac{(2003-m)+m}{m(2003-m)}\\right)\\\\\n&amp;=\\sum_{m=668}^{1001}\\left(\\frac{2003}{m(2003-m)}\\right)\\\\\n&amp;=2003\\sum_{m=668}^{1001}\\left(\\frac1{m(2003-m)}\\right).\n\\end{align*}\nNotice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b910f4dafca80b54c6e7bedf63b6485eebff0764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> is prime, and the denominator can never contain any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b910f4dafca80b54c6e7bedf63b6485eebff0764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79f244d658a9f15bbc070ea1eba561eb010aada6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003-m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> has maximum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/b/e4be2a66ae6f10de00c4c1742fd1e59434966678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003-668=1335$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> has maximum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888c508062c09735bab7ff0e11e7dc80cc7580db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b910f4dafca80b54c6e7bedf63b6485eebff0764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> is a prime number greater than both of them. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/b/91b0fa1295848b9d0737571b4edf7784b8e5d234.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{m=668}^{1001}\\left(\\dfrac1{m(2003-m)}\\right)=\\dfrac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"219\" height=\"55\" /> for some relatively prime positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05ff8cb00d334f7046395ccdd97e1a341180bed0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{p}{q}=\\dfrac{2003a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"89\" height=\"42\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> cannot divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b910f4dafca80b54c6e7bedf63b6485eebff0764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/4/ab4f55183170d23949e26600721250c1398c1da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2003a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"38\" /> is already in simplest form. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e90e8b869bea0ca425573d21403ee7dfd0081036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=2003a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da6be3fd8fb980ac1bfe4b611714e76360aebd28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b910f4dafca80b54c6e7bedf63b6485eebff0764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2003$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Q. E. D.\n</p><p>~Yuhao2012\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017194257\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.019 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 93/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4510/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37136:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017194257 and revision id 286808. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}